data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":2,"delta":{"type":"input_json_delta","partial_json":"{\"kind\": \"decision\", \"title\": \"Choose cart storage: Redis or Postgres\", \"body\": \"Long carts overflow the 4 KB session cookie. Move carts to a server-side store keyed by a session ID in the cookie.\\n\\n- **Postgres (recommended):** durable, queryable for analytics and recovery emails, no new infrastructure if already in use. Costs slightly slower cart writes and a purge job for stale carts.\\n- **Redis:** fast, TTL-based expiry built in. Carts can be lost on restart or eviction unless persistence is configured, and it adds a system to run if you don't already have one.\", \"actions\": [{\"label\":\"Use Postgres\",\"kind\":\"resolve\",\"recommended\":true},{\"label\":\"Use Redis\",\"kind\":\"resolve\"}]}"}}

